-- title:
--   Full Σ-corner at level Nr with B-family pairing
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring, complete for its maximal-ideal adic topology, with finite residue field $k$; let $p$ be a prime with $p\neq 2$ and $p\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$. Let $\bar\rho$ be a two-dimensional residual Galois representation over $k$ (a monoid homomorphism from $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb Q}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ to $\mathrm{End}_k$ of a rank-two space, trivial on some finite level) which is absolutely irreducible, and assume the associated adic representation is ordinary at $p$: over each valuation subring lying over $p$ there is a line, a member of a basis, stable under the decomposition group and containing $(\rho(\sigma)-1)v$ for all inertia elements $\sigma$. Let $S$ be a finite set of primes with $p\in S$, $N\neq 0$ with $p\nmid N$ and all prime factors of $N$ in $S$, and $Smin\subseteq S$ with $p\in Smin$ such that for primes $q\neq p$ one has $q\in Smin$ exactly when $\bar\rho$ is ramified at $q$; assume every $q\in Smin$ with $q\neq p$ divides $N$, every prime $q\neq p$ outside $Smin$ dividing $N$ has $q^2\mid N$, no prime $q\neq p$ has $q^3\mid N$, and the adic representation is unipotent on inertia at each $q\in Smin$, $q\neq p$. Let $r$ be a prime with $r\geq 5$, $r\notin S$, $r\nmid Np$, $p\nmid r-1$, and $\mathrm{tr}\,\bar\rho(\sigma)^2\neq (r+1)^2$ for every Frobenius $\sigma$ at $r$ attached to a valuation subring lying over $r$; assume cusp forms of level $N$ and weight $2$ have an integral structure (the $\mathbb Z$-span of forms with integral $q$-coefficients spans over $\mathbb C$). Let $\theta_0$ be a ring homomorphism from the weight-two level-$N$ Hecke algebra anaemic outside $S$ to $k$ such that for every prime $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$ the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\mathrm{Frob}_\ell)$ is $X^2-\theta_0(T_\ell)X+\ell$, and let $\pi_{T_0}$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism from the localisation [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ₀`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131) to $\mathcal O$. The conclusion asserts the existence of: the subgroup $H_0\leq(\mathbb Z/Nr)^\times$ consisting of the units whose image in $\mathbb Z/r$ is $1$, together with a degree-one level comparison $h_{10}$ from $(Nr,\top)$ to $(Nr,H_0)$; a commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra $\mathbb T_0$, module-finite over $\mathcal O$, acting $\mathcal O$-compatibly on $H^1(Nr,H_0;\mathcal O)=\mathrm{Hom}(\Gamma_{H_0}(Nr)^{\mathrm{ab}},\mathcal O)$; a corner datum $cd_0$ for this action (an idempotent splitting of $\mathbb T_0$, an index, and a level pairing on the corner ring and corner module), with the corner module finite and free over $\mathcal O$; an $\mathcal O$-algebra isomorphism $e_0$ from the corner ring onto [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ₀`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131); an element $t_p$ of the corner ring; and functions $t_{\mathrm{full}}$, $c_{\mathrm{full}}$ on the generator type [`CohCarrier.Gen (N*r) S`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13) with values in $\mathbb T_0$ and in $\mathcal O$; together with the inclusion $h_{W_0}$ of the corner submodule into the image, under the degeneracy map $iDegL$, of the parabolic homomorphisms at level $\Gamma(Nr)$ with $H=\top$, such that: (i) for primes $\ell$ with $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$, $\ell\nmid Nr$, the element $e_0^{-1}$ of the image of $T_\ell$ acts on the corner module as $heckeT$ at $\ell$; (ii) $t_p$ is a unit and acts both as $heckeT$ and as $heckeTlower$ at $p$; (iii) the torsion submodule of the corner module by the kernel of $\pi_{T_0}\circ e_0$ is non-zero, and the $\mathcal O$-rank of the corner module is the product of its rank with the rank of the corner ring; (iv) every $t\in\mathbb T_0$ acts as an element of the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra generated by the whole operator family `opFamily`, and even by the image of those generators $g$ which are not of the form $U_q$ with $q\nmid N$; (v) for such $g$, $t_{\mathrm{full}}(g)$ acts as `opFamily` at $g$ and $t_{\mathrm{full}}(g)-c_{\mathrm{full}}(g)$ lies in the ideal $\mathfrak m$ of the splitting at the chosen index; (vi) any $v\in H^1$ for which, for each such $g$ and each $k$, some power $(t_{\mathrm{full}}(g)-c_{\mathrm{full}}(g))^n$ carries $v$ into $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}^k\cdot H^1$ lies in the corner submodule; (vii) $c_{\mathrm{full}}(U_q)\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$ for primes $q\mid Nr$ with $q\mid N$, $q\neq p$, $q^2\mid N$; the residue of $c_{\mathrm{full}}(T_\ell)$ is $\theta_0(T_\ell)$ for $\ell$ as in (i); $c_{\mathrm{full}}(U_p)$ is a unit whenever $p\mid Nr$ and $p\mid N$ (a clause vacuous under $p\nmid N$); and $c_{\mathrm{full}}(\langle d\rangle)-1\in\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$ for all $d$; (viii) the corner ring acts faithfully on the corner module, and every $\sigma\in\Gamma_0(Nr)$ acts trivially, through $diamondRaw$, on the corner submodule; (ix) there is a prime $\ell_0\nmid Nrp$ such that for every irreducible $\varpi\in\mathcal O$ and every $v$ in the corner module, $heckeT_{\ell_0}v-(\ell_0+1)v\in\varpi\cdot H^1$ forces $v\in\varpi\cdot(\text{corner module})$; and (x) the pairing of $cd_0$ agrees with the chosen pairing family [`CuspForm.Bfam 𝒪`](def/CuspForm_CornerPairingFamily.html#L57) at $(Nr,H_0,h_{10})$ on corner elements viewed through $h_{W_0}$.
--
--   This is the level-raising rung at the residue characteristic: it realises the localised weight-two Hecke algebra of level $N$ anaemic outside $S$ as the corner ring of an operator algebra acting on the group cohomology of $\Gamma_{H_0}(Nr)=\Gamma_0(N)\cap\Gamma_1(r)$, with the corner module free over $\mathcal O$, the corner pairing identified with the universal $B$-family, and the full list of Hecke, $U$- and diamond normalisations needed downstream. It feeds the refinement that adds the further pinning data, [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_h1CornerData_fullCorner_sigmaPin_pairing_eq_bfam_and_free`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_h1CornerData_fullCorner_sigmaPin_pairing_eq_bfam_and_free).
